                <pb facs="0440" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.124A/44: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wharton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-24T18:00:00-04:00">July 24, 1929—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>26. Department’s 22, July 18, 5 p.m. Rockefeller Foundation advises that its
                    commission in Lagos has been authorized to send one of its staff to Monrovia
                    upon receipt of an invitation from the Liberian Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
